From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] fiq_debugger: make tty-output wakeups lossless and bound stall latency

The serial prompt (a tty write without trailing newline) still stalls
after a few characters: it only completes when the next serial input
event re-enters the tty path.  Two hardening changes:

1. tty_write() wakes the console thread unconditionally.  The
   conditional wake in wake_up_console_thread() exists to avoid a
   pi_lock/console_lock deadlock for the printk path; tty writes run
   in process context without the console lock, so the restriction
   does not apply and only loses wakeups here.

2. The console thread sleeps with a 20 ms timeout instead of an
   unbounded schedule(), so any wakeup lost on a path not covered by
   the explicit wakes self-heals within 20 ms instead of stalling
   until serial input arrives.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/rk_fiq_debugger.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/fiq_debugger/rk_fiq_debugger.c
@@ -374,7 +374,13 @@
 				smp_store_mb(console_thread_running, true);
 				continue;
 			}
-			schedule();
+			/*
+			 * Bounded sleep: if any wakeup is ever lost on a
+			 * path the explicit wakes do not cover, output
+			 * resumes after at most this delay instead of
+			 * stalling until the next serial input.
+			 */
+			schedule_timeout(msecs_to_jiffies(20));
 			smp_store_mb(console_thread_running, true);
 		}
 		if (kthread_should_stop())
@@ -466,7 +472,15 @@
 
 		if (ret <= 0)
 			return 0;
-		wake_up_console_thread(t->console_task);
+		/*
+		 * tty writes run in process context and never hold the
+		 * console lock, so the conditional wakeup in
+		 * wake_up_console_thread() (an anti-deadlock measure
+		 * for the printk path) is not needed here.  Wake the
+		 * console thread unconditionally so no user-visible
+		 * output can lose its wakeup.
+		 */
+		wake_up_process(t->console_task);
 	}
 	return count;
 }
